WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.493
Euler wrote most

00:00:01.305 --> 00:00:01.906
of his work

00:00:01.777 --> 00:00:02.979
after going blind

00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:04.759
Leonhard Euler lost

00:00:04.571 --> 00:00:05.149
one eye at

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:06.069
thirty-one and the

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:07.047
other at fifty-nine

00:00:07.189 --> 00:00:08.309
then kept working

00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:10.115
54 percent of the

00:00:09.927 --> 00:00:10.669
works in the

00:00:10.481 --> 00:00:11.671
standard catalogue

00:00:11.483 --> 00:00:12.367
of his writings

00:00:12.356 --> 00:00:13.193
came after his

00:00:13.005 --> 00:00:14.172
second eye failed

00:00:13.995 --> 00:00:15.811
in 1766

00:00:16.334 --> 00:00:17.536
He raised 13

00:00:17.348 --> 00:00:18.055
children

00:00:18.256 --> 00:00:19.211
often working with

00:00:19.023 --> 00:00:19.753
a baby on

00:00:19.565 --> 00:00:20.249
his lap

00:00:20.426 --> 00:00:21.145
and it took

00:00:20.957 --> 00:00:22.760
79 years after his

00:00:22.572 --> 00:00:23.716
death to finish

00:00:23.527 --> 00:00:24.447
printing what he

00:00:24.259 --> 00:00:24.977
left

00:00:25.494 --> 00:00:26.508
Full story on

00:00:26.319 --> 00:00:27.215
the dashboard
